Future-perspective review complete and saved to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Michael-Jordan/2026-08-14_020004/future.md` (SHA verified against context.json before reading).

**Verdict:** revise — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. **Blockers: 1, concerns: 5.**

**Strongest hit:** the piece is structurally built to age — absolute dates throughout, no static net-worth figure, a thesis that survives removal of every 2025-26 event, and a grievance-ledger table that absorbs future news by appending a row instead of rotting.

**The blocker (FUTURE-R1):** the coin-toss shrug is inverted. The draft has Jordan shrugging at security guards when he won; in the documented Last Dance scene, guard John Michael Wozniak won the $20 quarters bet and did the shrug at Jordan (packet S-19/S-25 confirm the contradiction). The corrected version is actually stronger for the thesis.

**Highest-priority concern (FUTURE-R2):** "got their six charters back for 2026" states a permanent settlement outcome as a one-season fix — by August 2027 the article's own growth-arrow evidence will read as possibly expired, when the settlement made charters effectively permanent.

Research note that sharpened two findings: the Wilbon "ESPN got panicky" item verified externally (Yahoo, The Spun, Awful Announcing), but Wilbon's actual point was that the panic was overblown because Jordan's NBC role is segments from a single pre-taped interview — which cuts against the draft's "settling into a broadcasting chair" framing. Also, Steve Kerr signed a multi-year extension in May 2026, so "now coaches the Warriors" is factually safe; only the write-date-anchored phrasing needs a touch. A concrete twelve-month refresh list is in the artifact.
